"Serves decode from quantized copies of attention weights that ship un-quantized (bf16): 8-bit for most layers, 4-bit for the last fifth, where quantization error matters far less. Models like poolside Laguna decode ~25% faster overall. Slightly lossy: replies can differ in wording from the exact bf16 decode, but measured answers stay the same quality (prompt reading and speculative checks keep the exact weights). Flipping this ON (rather than leaving it untouched) also enables DeepSeek-V4's compressor-input requant — ~7% faster decode there, with rare wording-level artifacts. Models with fully quantized attention are unaffected. Turn off for bit-exact bf16 decoding." = "用注意力权重的量化副本来做解码，而这些权重本身以未量化（bf16）的形式提供：大多数层用 8-bit，最后五分之一用 4-bit，那里的量化误差影响小得多。像 poolside Laguna 这样的模型整体解码快约 25%。略有损失：回复措辞可能与精确的 bf16 解码不同，但实测答案质量不变（提示词读取和投机校验仍使用精确权重）。把它打开（而不是保持不动）还会启用 DeepSeek-V4 的 compressor 输入重新量化 —— 那里的解码快约 7%，偶有措辞层面的瑕疵。注意力已完全量化的模型不受影响。要按位精确的 bf16 解码请关闭它。";
